# 134 - ASSOCIATIVITY within one rung, which §2 pins the precedence of but not
# the associativity of. Filed as bd_30-agents-2jk.54; this file assumes LEFT
# associativity for every binary rung, which is Rust's own and consistent with
# §2's "Rust's semantics" rule for / and %. Each line is a different answer,
# not a different error, under the other reading:
#   1 - 2 - 3     left -4    right  2
#   12 / 3 / 2    left  2    right 12   (12 / (3 / 2) is 12 / 1)
#   10 - 2 + 1    left  9    right  7   (mixed operators, same rung)
#   23 % 10 % 4   left  3    right  1   (23 % (10 % 4) is 23 % 2)
# The matching wrong-answer forms are all written out in 135.
--- source
print 1 - 2 - 3;
print 12 / 3 / 2;
print 10 - 2 + 1;
print 23 % 10 % 4;
--- expect
-4
2
9
3
